{"figure_index": 1, "page_no": 4, "caption": "Figure 1: BFT enhances the outputs of DeepSeek-R1-Distill series (14B, 32B and 70B). a : In the medical domain, theme-wise evaluation. b : In the medical domain, axis-wise evaluation. c : Forgetting evaluation in the general domain. We evaluated the general capabilities of LLMs previously fine-tuned on the OpenAI Health Bench Consensus subset using the MMLU benchmark. d : Forgetting evaluation in the general domain. We evaluated the general capabilities of LLMs previously fine-tuned on the OpenAI Health Bench Consensus subset using the CMMLU benchmark. e : In the biology domain, we applied BFT (blue) and SFT (orange) to fine-tune DeepSeek-R1-Distill series (14B, 32B and 70B). We evaluated LLMs on three biological process reasoning benchmarks. We evaluate ROUGE scores (recall-oriented understudy for gisting evaluation) between the generated final pathway names and ground truths, specifically ROUGE-L (longest common subsequence), ROUGE-1 (1-gram) and ROUGE-2 (2-gram) scores. f : We compared the BFT-based DeepSeek-R1-Distill (70B) against the latest baselines for biological process reasoning.", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel scientific figure composed of bar charts comparing model performance across tasks, model sizes, datasets, and methods.\n\nVisible panels and labels:\n- Panel **a**: Three grouped bar charts titled **Theme-wise (70B)**, **Theme-wise (32B)**, and **Theme-wise (14B)**. Y-axis is **Score**. X-axis compares **BFT** and **SFT**. Legend includes themes: `emergency_referrals`, `communication`, `hedging`, `complex_responses`, `health_data_tasks`, `global_health`, and `context_seeking`.\n- Panel **b**: Three grouped bar charts titled **Axis-wise (70B)**, **Axis-wise (32B)**, and **Axis-wise (14B)**. Y-axis is **Score**. X-axis compares **BFT** and **SFT**. Legend includes axes: `communication_quality`, `instruction_following`, `accuracy`, `context_awareness`, and `completeness`.\n- Panel **c**: Three grouped bar charts titled **MMLU (70B)**, **MMLU (32B)**, and **MMLU (14B)**. Y-axis is **Accuracy**. Categories include **STEM**, **Sociology**, **Humanities**, and **Other**. Legend compares **Base**, **BFT**, and **SFT**.\n- Panel **d**: Three grouped bar charts titled **CMMLU (70B)**, **CMMLU (32B)**, and **CMMLU (14B)**. Y-axis is **Accuracy**. Categories include **STEM**, **Sociology**, **Humanities**, and **Other**. Legend compares **Base**, **BFT**, and **SFT**.\n- Panel **e**: Nine grouped bar charts for summarization-style metrics across model sizes **14B**, **32B**, and **70B**. Metrics are **Rouge-L**, **Rouge-1**, and **Rouge-2**. X-axis datasets include **MsigDB**, **NeST**, and **Gene Ontology**. Legend compares **BFT** and **SFT**.\n- Panel **f**: Three grouped bar charts titled **MsigDB**, **NeST**, and **Gene Ontology**. Metrics on the x-axis are **Rouge-L**, **Rouge-1**, and **Rouge-2**. Legend compares methods **BFT**, **GeneAgent**, and **GPT-Hu**. Error bars are shown.\n\nBiological source objects:\n- The figure explicitly references biological or biomedical knowledge sources/datasets: **MSigDB**, **NeST**, and **Gene Ontology**.\n- No microscopy images, organisms, cells, tissues, molecules, or anatomical structures are visually shown.\n\nTransformations/model interfaces:\n- The figure compares model variants and training/finetuning conditions labeled **Base**, **BFT**, and **SFT** across model sizes **14B**, **32B**, and **70B**.\n- It presents quantitative evaluation outputs as grouped bar plots with accuracy, score, and ROUGE metrics.\n\nFindings visible from the figure:\n- Theme-wise and axis-wise scores vary substantially by model size and training condition.\n- MMLU and CMMLU accuracy are compared across subject groups for Base, BFT, and SFT.\n- ROUGE-based performance is shown for biomedical/gene-related datasets, with BFT and SFT compared in panel e and BFT/GeneAgent/GPT-Hu compared with error bars in panel f."]}

